  "the_3d_walkthrough_sold_us_instantly_w.0591": "The 3D walkthrough sold us instantly — we could feel the light and the space before a single wall went up.",
  "the_approach_the_terrace_and_the_view.f091": "The approach, the terrace, and the view the house was planned around.",
  "the_brick_shell_before_and_after_cut_t.d245": "The brick shell before and after, cut together.",
  "the_brief_asked_for_a_studio_with_no_p.8801": "The brief asked for a studio with no private offices at all. A single twelve-metre table runs the length of the floor and everything else — meeting rooms, library, making space — is arranged loosely around it.",
  "the_building_had_six_floors_and_one_li.2c94": "The building had six floors and one lift core, which meant nobody met anyone from another floor. A single cut through the slabs allowed a stair to link all six.",
  "the_cheapest_and_greenest_square_metre.94c4": "The cheapest and greenest square metre is the one you do not build. We would rather rework what is already standing — open it up, insulate it properly, and keep the parts that give the place its character.",
  "the_cheapest_and_greenest_square_metre.f07b": "The cheapest and greenest square metre is the one you do not build. We would rather rework what exists than add to it.",
  "the_coffee_and_the_wall.f258": "The coffee and the wall",
  "the_contact_page_has_a_short_form_tell.6947": "The contact page has a short form — tell us what you are thinking of and one of us will reply.",
  "the_core_is_clad_in_copper_that_will_d.7fc1": "The core is clad in copper that will darken over the next decade. Around it the palette stays deliberately quiet: lime plaster, oak boards and blackened steel.",
  "the_craft.f06b": "The craft",
  "the_crane_rail_runs_the_full_length_of.8f41": "The crane rail runs the full length of the hall and was the one thing the tenants asked us not to touch. Every new partition stops short of it.",
  "the_design_office.922b": "The design office",
  "the_drafting_hall_desks_along_the_nort.a892": "The drafting hall, desks along the north windows",
  "the_drafting_hall_the_model_shop_and_t.fb1f": "The drafting hall, the model shop and the materials library. Client meetings happen here, at the long table.",
  "the_drawing_wall.05de": "The drawing wall",
  "the_first_conversation_is_free_and_cos.7c0c": "The first conversation is free and costs you nothing but an hour. Bring a plan, a photograph, a rough budget, or just the thing you keep thinking about.",
  "the_first_house_that_has_ever_truly_fe.4bbc": "\"The first house that has ever truly felt like ours.\"",
  "the_flat_had_the_harbour_on_three_side.108a": "The flat had the harbour on three sides and no sense of arrival at all. The entry now runs through a deliberately low, dark hall before the space opens.",
  "the_foundry.3118": "The Foundry",
  "the_garden_the_approach_the_terrace_an.f1c3": "The garden, the approach, the terrace and the parking are part of the building, not an afterthought once the scaffolding comes down. Drawn at the same time as the house, they make the whole thing feel settled.",
  "the_house_is_clad_in_charred_timber_an.aeac": "The house is clad in charred timber and reads almost black from the approach. At its centre a double-height room is finished entirely in pale birch.",
  "the_kettle_works_and_the_long_table_is.9bf8": "The kettle works and the long table is usually free. Bring a plan, a photograph, or just an idea you cannot shake.",
  "the_kit.3ed1": "The kit",
  "the_lantern_lit_at_dusk_seen_from_the.de82": "The lantern lit at dusk, seen from the garden.",
  "the_long_table_filling_up_over_a_worki.cb55": "The long table filling up over a working morning.",
