  "the_project_page_has_the_full_story_an.8a74": "The project page has the full story and the photographs.",
  "the_quiet_stretch_plans_sections_detai.3570": "The quiet stretch. Plans, sections, details. The rule is no meetings before eleven, and it mostly survives contact with reality.",
  "the_result_is_a_house_you_walk_down_th.e724": "The result is a house you walk down through. Every pavilion has its own outlook and the excavation was reduced to almost nothing.",
  "the_roof_is_a_light_steel_grid_carried.b0e8": "The roof is a light steel grid carried on the existing walls, so neither building needed strengthening.",
  "the_site_is_long_narrow_and_faces_away.93e3": "The site is long, narrow and faces away from the water, so the house turns its back on the street and opens along its length instead. Every principal room reaches daylight from two directions.",
  "the_site_studio.42b0": "The site studio",
  "the_space.6752": "The space",
  "the_studio_began_in_2009_with_one_hous.958d": "The studio began in 2009 with one house and a conviction that has not changed since: a building should be shaped by the life inside it, not the other way round. That first client wanted somewhere to cook, read and have people over — so we designed around a kitchen and let the rest follow.",
  "the_studio_is_open.ccec": "The studio is open:",
  "the_studios_are_built_as_freestanding.5241": "The studios are built as freestanding boxes, so the original volume is still legible from end to end above them.",
  "the_two_halves_of_the_site_had_never_b.fe7c": "The two halves of the site had never been connected. Roofing the yard between them created a single atrium that now does all the circulation for both.",
  "the_warehouse.364a": "The Warehouse",
  "the_window_seat_was_the_client_s_one_r.0012": "The window seat was the client’s one request. It is deeper than it needs to be, and it is where the family now eats most meals.",
  "there_are_two_studios.3857": "There are two studios:",
  "they_breathed_new_life_into_a_tired_ol.4af3": "They breathed new life into a tired old building without losing an ounce of its character. Genuinely remarkable work.",
  "they_listened_to_how_we_actually_live.06e0": "They listened to how we actually live, then gave us a home that fits us perfectly — every room has a reason to be there.",
  "this_is_architecture_that_reflects_all.2562": "This is architecture that reflects all of you",
  "three_benches_br_we_could_not_work_wit.9a80": "Three benches<br>we could not work without.",
  "three_linked_pavilions_stepping_down_a.9a84": "Three linked pavilions stepping down a slope, each following the contour it sits on.",
  "three_steps_br_about_two_weeks.567a": "Three steps,<br>about two weeks.",
  "through_the_trees_to_the_porch_in_late.42e5": "Through the trees to the porch, in late autumn.",
